# Playwright E2E Rules

- Cover critical user journeys first (auth, lead CRUD, search/filter, primary navigation).
- Write behavior-focused test names and group by feature with `test.describe`.
- Prefer semantic selectors (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`, `getByTestId`) over CSS/XPath.
- Use Playwright auto-waiting assertions (`toBeVisible`, `toHaveURL`, `toHaveText`); avoid hard sleeps.
- Keep tests deterministic by mocking unstable external dependencies when needed.
- Validate both success and failure paths (validation errors, network failures, empty states).
- Keep each spec focused and maintainable; avoid giant all-in-one scenario files.

## Example
```ts
await page.getByTestId("login-submit").click();
await expect(page).toHaveURL(/dashboard/);
```
